{# narrative_engine/plot_slot — who, where or what fills one slot of a step.
   Asked by PlotPlanning for each slot with more than one candidate, and
   by PickAgent for the agent. The answer is a candidate key, c1 onward.
   Receives: mastermind { name }, scheme, finish (how the scheme is
     meant to end; may be empty), step (the step, as a record plot_step
     words with each unfilled slot shown as its name in brackets), purpose
     (what the step is for in the plan, worded by plot_purpose), slot (the
     name being filled), kind (person, place or thing), options [{ key,
     name, occupation, relation, lives, named, self }]: who or what each
     candidate is and, for a person, why they are on the list. `relation`
     is how the mastermind knows them, a PlotMenus::RelationId; `lives`
     where a stranger lives; `self` the mastermind doing it in person.
   NOTE: no fenced blocks and no literal braces anywhere in this file. #}
[ state scheme ]
{{ mastermind.name }} is working toward this: {{ scheme }}{% if length(finish) > 0 %}
It is meant to end with this: {{ finish }}{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state step ]
{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_step.prompt" %}
{% include "components/narrative_engine/plot_purpose.prompt" %}
[ end state ]

[ question pick choice ]
{% if kind == "place" %}Where should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`?{% else if kind == "thing" %}What should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`?{% else %}Who should [{{ slot }}] be in the step in `step`, to best serve the scheme in `scheme`? Prefer the person the scheme, or how it is meant to end, plainly names for this part of the step, if they are on the list.{% endif %}
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}{{ o.key }}: {{ o.name }}{% if o.self %} themselves{% endif %}{% if length(o.occupation) > 0 %}, {{ o.occupation }}{% endif %}{% if length(o.relation) > 0 or length(o.lives) > 0 or o.named %} ({% if o.relation == "close_and_colleague" %}someone they know, in the same organisation{% else if o.relation == "close" %}someone they know{% else if o.relation == "colleague" %}in the same organisation{% else if o.relation == "neighbour" %}lives in the same hold{% else if length(o.lives) > 0 %}lives in {{ o.lives }}{% endif %}{% if o.named %}{% if length(o.relation) > 0 or length(o.lives) > 0 %}; {% endif %}named in the scheme{% endif %}){% endif %}
{% endfor %}[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
